(1645, 2, 'AUDIO_MCQ', 'Listen to two people talking about traditional public libraries versus modern digital e-readers. Who expresses these opinions?', 'Man: There\'s an undeniable treasure in municipal libraries—their physical archives preserve local historical manuscripts and maps that simply cannot be digitized. But when traveling for business, digital e-readers offer unbeatable convenience; carrying fifty books on a lightweight slate is extraordinary.\nWoman: I agree that e-readers are a marvel for traveling, but public libraries foster social cohesion in neighborhoods that no electronic bookstore can replicate. That said, instant digital borrowing on e-readers has undeniably prompted people to read far more frequently than when they had to wait for library opening hours.', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 'prompt', 'null', '0340a42b-e991-4f57-bcd9-f570f421c972', 'set8'),
(1650, 2, 'AUDIO_MCQ', 'Listen to an arts correspondent on the radio reviewing an interactive immersive projection exhibition.', 'Arts Correspondent: Stepping into the digital gallery space at the Light Pavilion was an astonishing experience. The seamless architectural mapping of Van Gogh\'s brushstrokes across forty-foot curved walls created a breathtaking sensory world that made visitors feel immersed inside the paintings themselves. However, as an arts critic, I cannot overlook the broader trend. Too many interactive exhibitions prioritize superficial spectacle and selfie backdrops over genuine artistic depth and curation. Spectacle without historical context leaves audiences dazzled but unenlightened.', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 'prompt', 'null', 'e5fbe85b-3ba6-437f-9c12-c8270cf5c71c', 'set8'),
(1653, 2, 'AUDIO_MCQ', 'Listen to an international conference director on the radio discussing the organization of global corporate conventions.', 'Conference Director: Orchestrating an international corporate summit with delegates arriving from forty countries requires immense operational discipline. While speakers and venues draw headlines, establishing redundant digital streaming infrastructure is the single most vital logistical priority—if your satellite feed drops during a global announcement, the entire convention fails. Looking at hybrid event design, organizers must realize that engaging remote delegates requires completely different presentation formats than live stage talks. An online audience loses attention after twenty minutes of a podium monologue; you must weave interactive polling and breakout hubs into the digital broadcast.', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 'prompt', 'null', '9a61475e-6eb5-4b95-bd81-16349bdd7cf9', 'set8'),
