(1318, 4, 'QUESTION_FORM', 'The Panama Canal Project', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 'click', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1319, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 1:\n\nEngineers initially debated whether a sea-level cut or an elevated lock system offered the most viable blueprint across the continental divide. Chief planners recognized that torrential rains and swelling river basins would make an unrestricted sea-level trench continually prone to collapse. Critics countered that constructing colossal concrete lock chambers and damming torrential rivers was impractical and dangerous. Planners insisted that a lock-and-lake system could safely regulate water volumes while handling massive transport vessels. This mechanical doctrine became the foundational blueprint for construction.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1320, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 2:\n\nThe landscape underwent extreme reconfiguration as steam shovels and dynamite carved deep chasms through solid volcanic basalt. Specialized dredging equipment cleared millions of cubic yards of mud from tropical riverbeds. Miles of temporary rail lines were laid to haul excavation rubble across treacherous slopes. Workers lived under spartan conditions in hastily erected barracks, requiring unprecedented supply logistics. Fleets of freight ships delivered tens of thousands of concrete barrels, structural steel gates, heavy steam boilers, and preserved rations to feed the enormous workforce.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1321, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 3:\n\nA specialized medical corps—comprising epidemiologists, sanitary inspectors, and laboratory technicians—was assembled under military medical command. Their essential task involved eradicating the deadly outbreaks of yellow fever and malaria that had decimated previous French efforts. Armed with fumigation sprayers, window screens, and oil treatments for stagnant pools, this health division transformed the deadly jungle corridor into a habitable industrial zone.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1322, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 4:\n\nExcavation reached its peak at the formidable Culebra Cut, where unstable earthen mountains continually slid into freshly dug trenches. Unpredictable rockslides obliterated railbeds and crushed heavy machinery overnight, yet work resumed after each disaster without pause. By the summer of 1913, the primary excavations linked both sides of the isthmus, and water was released to fill Gatun Lake. In August 1914, the cargo steamship SS Ancon made the historic maiden crossing, successfully navigating the locks just as international tensions escalated into global conflict.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1323, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 5:\n\nThe completion of the canal provoked both international acclaim and sharp economic debates among trading nations. Some European shippers complained about steep transit tolls and questioned whether the project justified its immense financial and human toll. Others argued that the operational schedule favored specific geopolitical routes. However, global trade figures soon demonstrated that the shortcut slashed thousands of ocean miles, permanently transforming global supply lines.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1324, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 6:\n\nIn the decades following the canal’s opening, maritime authorities implemented continuous structural expansions to accommodate ever-growing vessel dimensions. Later engineering teams deepened channels, installed computer-guided towing locomotives, and constructed massive third-lane locks. Modern marine historians frequently retrace these construction feats through archival photographs, documenting the human endurance required to conquer the continental barrier.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
(1325, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 7:\n\nThe dramatic story of the canal’s creation has endured as an icon of twentieth-century technological achievement. Countless documentaries, engineering treatises, and historic exhibits recount the epic scale of the excavation. Today, the canal remains under sovereign Panamanian administration, safeguarded as an indispensable artery of international commerce and a globally recognized historic landmark.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', '5a6b3500-f13e-43f3-a015-4bdcda53c9d1', 'set6'),
