(1506, 4, 'QUESTION_FORM', 'Read the passage quickly. Choose a heading from the list for each numbered paragraph. There is one heading that you do not need. The first one is done for you.', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 'click', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1507, 4, 'QUESTION_FORM', 'The Voyage of HMS Beagle', NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 'click', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1508, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 1:\n\nCaptain FitzRoy believed that an extensive coastal survey could produce infallible maritime charts while accumulating geological evidence supporting biblical creation. He maintained that accurate chronological measurements using precision chronometers would revolutionize navigation. However, academic skeptics warned that embarking on a prolonged voyage aboard an overcrowded vessel was exceedingly risky. They insisted that erratic Pacific currents and harsh coastal gales would inevitably endanger the vessel. FitzRoy held firm that meticulous hydrographic surveying could unlock safe sea lanes.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1509, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 2:\n\nThe vessel had been extensively modified prior to departure, receiving an extra upper deck and copper sheathing along the wooden hull to resist tropical shipworms. Because of its small dimensions, every cubic foot was strictly allocated. The quarters were remarkably confined, forcing officers and scientists to sleep in hammocks slung among survey equipment. Immense provisions were stowed below: casks of salted beef, barrels of ship’s biscuits, lemon juice to ward off scurvy, and specialized packaging materials for preserving animal and plant specimens.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1510, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 3:\n\nThe specialized onboard surveying team—consisting of draftsmen, seasoned navigators, an instrument technician, and Darwin himself—worked with focused discipline. Their scientific inventory was advanced for the era, encompassing marine chronometers, compound microscopes, geological hammers, and chemical jars, which Darwin used continuously to record rock strata and catalog terrestrial specimens.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1511, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 4:\n\nThe ship navigated violent equatorial squalls before surveying the rugged contours of the South American coastline over several arduous years. Long inland expeditions across the Argentine pampas and the Andes Mountains yielded fossils of colossal extinct mammals. By the autumn of 1835, the Beagle reached the isolated Galápagos archipelago. Here Darwin collected diverse mockingbirds, finches, and giant tortoises, noting subtle physical variations across nearby islands before the ship commenced its Pacific crossing and returned home in 1836.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1512, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 5:\n\nDarwin’s return generated immediate enthusiasm alongside sharp scientific disagreements within Victorian academies. Conservative geologists questioned his radical deductions regarding gradual land uplift and fossil distribution. Others disputed his anatomical classifications of island fauna. Nevertheless, leading taxonomists verified that Darwin’s specimens represented distinct, previously unclassified species, prompting scientists to rethink the permanence of biological forms.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1513, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 6:\n\nIn the decades following the Beagle’s return, subsequent survey expeditions revisited South American waters using steam-powered vessels and modern sounding apparatus. Modern marine biologists have repeatedly retraced the Beagle’s exact sea coordinates to examine ecological transformations, producing celebrated scientific television series highlighting Darwin’s route.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
(1514, 4, 'MCQ', 'Paragraph 7:\n\nThe legacy of the Beagle voyage has left an indelible mark on intellectual history. Darwin’s captivating travel diary, The Voyage of the Beagle, was published in 1839 and became an enduring international classic. His later evolutionary thesis transformed global science. Today, replicas of the vessel and preserved specimen collections housed in national museums continue to inspire researchers around the world.', NULL, NULL, 2, 0, NULL, 'select', 'null', 'caf412a0-5136-421e-a2f7-41efa2f270d7', 'set7'),
